# Qwen3.6-27B-FP8 — LAZY-mode / HPU-graphs SPEED test (the lever we wrote off prematurely).
# We run EAGER because LAZY (=1) died compiling the hybrid+fp8+vision WARMUP graph (synStatus 26 in
# HabanaFusedOpLazy warmup_graphs). BUT we now run VLLM_SKIP_WARMUP=true regardless — which SKIPS
# warmup_graphs entirely. So lazy may load + compile graphs ON-DEMAND at first request and serve. If it
# works, HPU graphs eliminate the per-op host-launch overhead (64 layers × 8 ranks × every token = the
# eager wall) → potentially a large SS + concurrency win. + PT_HPU_ENABLE_LAZY_COLLECTIVES graphs the
# TP-8 all-reduce (the 397B-sslazy8 win). util 0.10 (graphs need capture room; this is a SPEED test, not
# a footprint test — optimize memory AFTER if it wins). GATES: serve up + COHERENT (lazy fused-op may
# still synStatus-26 at first request; the coherence gate catches it) + SS c1 > eager 33.1 / dynshapes 39.1.
IMAGE=vllm-gaudi:next
MODEL_PATH=Qwen3.6-27B-FP8
SERVED_NAME=qwen36-27b
MODEL_ENV="-e PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=1 -e PT_HPU_WEIGHT_SHARING=0 -e VLLM_SKIP_WARMUP=true -e PT_HPU_ENABLE_LAZY_COLLECTIVES=true -e VLLM_ENGINE_ITERATION_TIMEOUT_S=1800 -e VLLM_RPC_TIMEOUT=100000000 -e VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600 -e VLLM_GRAPH_RESERVED_MEM=0.10 -e VLLM_HPU_LOG_STEP_CPU_FALLBACKS=true"
VLLM_ARGS="--quantization fp8 --kv-cache-dtype fp8_inc --tensor-parallel-size 8 --max-model-len 2048 --max-num-seqs 16 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.10 --block-size 128 --async-scheduling --no-enable-prefix-caching --trust-remote-code"
